Well done, lady.
干得好，女士。

316
00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:31.820
Thank you.
谢谢。

317
00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.640
And finally, Angela's journal.
最后，是安吉拉的日记。

318
00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.720
Lady, we got a lot of mail, a lot of requests.
女士，我们收到了很多邮件和请求。

319
00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:42.820
Melina from Idaho said, when is Angela going to read from her journals again?
来自爱达荷州的梅琳娜问，安吉拉什么时候会再读她的日记？

320
00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.500
It always makes me laugh out loud.
那总是让我大笑出声。

321
00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.300
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

322
00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.920
So, Ange, I wrote you.
所以，安吉，我给你写信了。

323
00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.100
I said, can you read from your journal today?
我说，你今天能读读你的日记吗？

324
00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.020
Yes, I can.
可以，我能读。

325
00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:50.820
I can.
我可以。

326
00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:52.420
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

327
00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.960
I have some Angela journal updates for everyone.
我有一些关于安吉拉日记的最新消息要告诉大家。

328
00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.260
What are they?
是什么消息？

329
00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:58.480
You know, we've been doing some home construction.
你知道，我们一直在进行房屋装修。

330
00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.620
And I haven't been able to get into our shed, where we keep everything, right?
我一直没法进入我们存放杂物的棚子，对吧？

331
00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.880
Finally got into the shed the other day.
前几天终于进去了。

332
00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:06.620
We're digging around.
我们在里面翻找。

333
00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.380
All I was looking for was some seasonal doormats that I kept.
我当时只是在找我收起来的季节性门垫。

334
00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.240
I found a little box that said, Angela's trailer.
结果发现了一个写着“安吉拉的拖车”的小盒子。

335
00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.920
Jenna, I didn't even find this when we were writing our book.
珍娜，我们在写书的时候都没发现这个。

336
00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.640
It had a blanket in it, a pillow.
里面有一条毯子，一个枕头。

337
00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:24.420
It had, like, some extra socks.
还有一些多余的袜子。

338
00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:28.040
Like, who knows how long this little box has been in the way back of the shed.
谁知道这个小盒子在棚子最里面放了多久了。

339
00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.340
But it had a journal that I kept in my trailer.
但里面有一本我在拖车里写的日记。

340
00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:36.320
And I wrote in it in the pilot, season one, and season two.
我在试播集、第一季和第二季期间写过它。

341
00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.260
Oh, my gosh, Angela.
天哪，安吉拉。

342
00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:38.740
I know.
我知道。

343
00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:39.780
This is such a find.
这真是个大发现。

344
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:40.700
It's such a find.
真是个大发现。

345
00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:43.140
I wrote about the basketball episode, lady.
我写了关于篮球那一集的内容，女士。

346
00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.020
You did not.
你居然写了。

347
00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.460
Like, all of these specific things.
就是所有这些具体的细节。

348
00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.960
I was, like, in journal overload.
我当时简直是日记过载了。

349
00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.540
I was like, oh, my God, what am I going to share all this?
我心想，天哪，我要把这些都分享出来吗？

350
00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:49.940
This is all.
这就是全部内容了。

351
00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:51.820
But I'm going to wait.
但我打算先留着。

352
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.660
I'm going to save those for special things.
我要把它们留给特别的事情。

353
00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.300
I wrote about filming the pilot.
我写过关于拍摄试播集的内容。

354
00:14:55.840 --> 00:15:00.000
I have little notes that, like, Oscar gave me taped inside the journal.
我的日记里贴着一些奥斯卡给我的小纸条。

355
00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.460
I have my call sheet, lady.
我有我的通告单，女士。

356
00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:03.500
Wow.
哇。

357
00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:04.480
I know.
我知道。

358
00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.220
And we found so much stuff when we did our book.
我们在做书的时候发现了好多东西。

359
00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:13.100
Is it making you want to call the publisher and say, we need to do a reprint?
这有没有让你想给出版商打电话说，我们需要加印？

360
00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:13.560
No.
没有。

361
00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.160
So I'm not going to read from that journal today.
所以我今天不打算读那本日记。

362
00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.080
I thought I would save that journal for when we get to the end of the run.
我想把那本日记留到我们剧集完结的时候再读。

363
00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.320
That's fun.
那很有趣。

364
00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:22.760
Yeah.
是啊。

365
00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:23.320
Okay.
好的。

366
00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.880
Because I also found a card you gave me.
因为我还发现了你给我的一张卡片。

367
00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:26.440
Oh.
噢。

368
00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:27.040
I know.
我知道。

369
00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.540
So I'm going to save all that.
所以我打算把那些都留着。

370
00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:34.500
But today's Angela's Journal, you guys, I have a journal that I titled Travel Journal.
但今天的安吉拉日记，伙计们，我有一本我命名为“旅行日记”的日记。

371
00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.480
Oh, it's a travel journal.
噢，是旅行日记啊。

372
00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:40.760
And I only wrote on it when I was on a plane or a bus or a train.
我只在坐飞机、大巴或火车时才会在上面写东西。

373
00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:45.640
And I guess, guys, I really take inventory of who sits around me.
我想，伙计们，我真的很喜欢盘点坐在我周围的人。

374
00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.100
You do, Ange.
你确实会，安吉。

375
00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:51.560
When you travel, you leave me the most amazing messages about the people you were surrounded
当你旅行时，你会给我留下关于你周围人的最精彩的留言，

376
00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:51.880
by.
关于他们的。

377
00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.940
It's so entertaining and detailed.
非常有趣且详尽。

378
00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:54.460
Okay.
好的。

379
00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.920
Well, here we go, you guys.
好吧，我们开始吧，伙计们。

380
00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.840
This is written at 5.56 p.m.
这是在下午5点56分写的，

381
00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:02.360
on a flight from Philadelphia to Los Angeles.
在从费城飞往洛杉矶的航班上。

382
00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.320
It was 2005.
那是2005年。

383
00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:05.320
Okay.
好的。

384
00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:05.900
Okay.
好的。

385
00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.040
I have now been on this flight for three hours.
我已经在这架飞机上待了三个小时了。

386
00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.280
I write, 5.56 p.m.
我写道，下午5点56分，

387
00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.400
in all caps, BORED!
用全大写字母写着，无聊！

388
00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:15.900
Exclamation point.
感叹号。

389
00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:21.880
And then I write, Ken Kuapis, the director of the office, actually has a movie on this
然后我写道，肯·卡皮斯，《办公室》的导演，这架飞机上居然放着他的电影。

390
00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:22.240
plane.
是《牛仔裤的夏天》。

391
00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.440
It's the Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants.
那是主打电影。

392
00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:26.120
It was the feature movie.
我刚上映时和珍娜在电影院看过，所以我不想花5美元买耳机。

393
00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.920
I saw it with Jenna at the theater when it came out, so I didn't feel like paying $5
皱眉表情。

394
00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.260
for headphones.
噢，是啊。

395
00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:33.640
Frowny face.
现在他们会提供耳机了。

396
00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:34.920
Oh, yeah.
是啊。

397
00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.780
Now they give you headphones.
这是在2005年。

398
00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:37.360
Yeah.
我接着写道，现在在放《单身公寓》，我真希望我有一副耳机。

399
00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.100
This is in 2005.
这是在2005年。

400
00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:44.300
I go on to say, and now the odd couple is on, and I wish I had a pair of headphones.
我接着写道，现在在放《单身公寓》，我真希望我有一副耳机。

401
00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:49.100
The guy behind me is pounding Jack Daniels and Coke.
我后面那个人在狂喝杰克丹尼兑可乐。

402
00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:51.160
I think he's finally passed out.
我想他终于喝断片了。

403
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.020
Oh, and the two ladies in front of me are feuding.
哦，还有我前面的两位女士在吵架。

404
00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:58.820
One wanted the other to switch so her husband could sit next to her, but the other lady said
其中一个想让另一个换座位，好让她丈夫能坐在她旁边，但另一位女士说

405
00:16:58.820 --> 00:16:59.160
no.
不行。

406
00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.580
She didn't want to give up her seat.
她不想让出自己的座位。

407
00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.600
It's been tense ever since.
从那以后气氛一直很紧张。

408
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.080
This is amazing.
这太有意思了。

409
00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.040
This part cracks me up.
这一段把我逗乐了。

410
00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:11.800
The guy next to me has been diligently reading a book on Texas Hold'em and furiously scribbling
我旁边那个人一直在认真读一本关于德州扑克的书，还疯狂地做着

411
00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:12.140
notes.
笔记。

412
00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.780
He ran out of paper and has started to write on his plane ticket.
他纸用完了，开始在机票上写。

413
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.600
He keeps covering his notes with his hand, like I'm going to steal his secrets.
他一直用手遮着笔记，好像我会偷看他的秘诀一样。

414
00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.620
I'd offer him a page out of this journal, but he's such a grump.
我本想给他一张这本日记的纸，但他脾气太臭了。

415
00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:30.060
We should be landing in half an hour, and I'm starving, and there's no snacks on U.S.
我们半小时后应该就能降落了，我饿坏了，而且全美航空没有免费零食，

416
00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:30.540
Airways
除非你想花7美元买。

417
00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:32.180
unless you want to pay $7.
太荒唐了。

418
00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:33.580
Ridiculous.
简直离谱。

419
00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.100
What happened to the airline industry?
航空业到底怎么了？

420
00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.580
Question mark, exclamation point.
问号，感叹号。

421
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.360
It was amazing, Angela.
太棒了，安吉拉。

422
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.560
Oh, you guys.
哦，你们俩。

423
00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.700
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

424
00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.840
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

425
00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.460
Can you believe I wouldn't give the guy a piece of paper?
你能相信我竟然没给那个人一张纸吗？

426
00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.400
He's like writing on his plane ticket.
他竟然在机票上写字。

427
00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:57.820
You're not going to give the airline $5 for headphones or $7 for a snack.
你既不愿花5美元买耳机，也不愿花7美元买零食。

428
00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.220
You're not sharing your paper.
你还不愿意分享你的纸。

429
00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:02.540
I'm not going to spend $12 on things I need.
我才不会花12美元买那些我需要的东西。

430
00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:03.240
No.
不买。

431
00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.360
Oh, ridiculous.
哦，太荒唐了。

432
00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.560
$7 for snacks.
零食要7美元。

433
00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:11.880
I absolutely loved it.
我真的太喜欢了。

434
00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:13.180
Well, there you go.
好吧，就是这样。

435
00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.940
That's my Angela's Journals updates.
这就是我的安吉拉日记更新。

436
00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:20.740
I will save some of our early years that I wrote about for the end of our run.
我会把我们早年间的一些经历留到节目快结束时再讲。

437
00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.980
That's all I got for Fast Facts, lady.
女士，这就是我所有的快讯了。

438
00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:27.100
I could really just do a whole episode of you reading your journals.
我真的可以专门做一期节目，让你读你的日记。

439
00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:31.580
You know what this made me want to do is journal again when I travel.
你知道这让我想要做什么吗？就是旅行时重新开始写日记。

440
00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.320
Because I used to always journal.
因为我以前总是写日记。

441
00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:34.260
Me too.
我也是。

442
00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:35.200
Yeah.
是啊。

443
00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.120
It's such good character study.
这是非常好的角色研究。

444
00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:40.800
If you're a writer or an actor, it's great character study.
如果你是作家或演员，这是极好的角色研究。

445
00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:45.520
I always love your messages when you've gotten off a plane because that's what they are.
我总是很喜欢你下飞机后发来的信息，因为它们就是这样。

446
00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.340
That's the description I get.
那就是我得到的描述。

447
00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.420
You really paint a picture.
你真的描绘出了一幅画面。

448
00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.140
All right.
好吧。

449
00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.140
Well, should we take a break?
那么，我们要休息一下吗？

450
00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.160
And then when we come back, does Stanley have a mustache?
等我们回来的时候，斯坦利留胡子了吗？

451
00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:56.040
Oh, there's a hot debate.
哦，这引发了一场激烈的争论。

452
00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:11.310
Well, the episode's going to start with Pam and Phyllis.
嗯，这一集是以帕姆和菲利斯开始的。

453
00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:16.610
They're passing around a card for everyone to sign, welcoming Stanley back from his tonsil
她们正在传阅一张卡片让大家签名，欢迎斯坦利做完扁桃体

454
00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.050
surgery.
手术后回来。

455
00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:23.970
I guess the card says, quote, glad they didn't mix up your tonsillectomy with a mustacheectomy.
我猜卡片上写着，引用一下，很高兴他们没把你的扁桃体切除术和胡子切除术搞混。

456
00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.330
We get some gym sass.
我们看到了一些吉姆的毒舌。

457
00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:27.490
He says, oh, that's not good.
他说，哦，那可不太好。

458
00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:29.130
Met with some Phyllis sass.
接着是菲利斯的毒舌回击。

459
00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.490
She's like, oh, because your jokes are all hilarious.
她说，哦，因为你的笑话都特别好笑。

460
00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:34.150
You know what, lady?
你知道吗，这位女士？

461
00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.710
This made me realize we really like a punny card on this show.
这让我意识到，我们这个节目真的很喜欢双关语卡片。

462
00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:38.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

463
00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:42.490
Remember in the Alliance, Meredith got a card that said, happy bird day?
还记得在《联盟》那一集里，梅雷迪思收到一张写着“生日快乐”的卡片吗？（注：英文原文为Happy Bird Day，利用Bird和Birth的谐音）

464
00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:43.010
Yep.
没错。

465
00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.230
Do you have a memory of getting a real pun card?
你有没有收到过真正的双关语卡片的记忆？

466
00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:46.890
Because I do.
因为我有。

467
00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:49.770
No, we give my dad pun cards.
没有，我们都是给我爸送双关语卡片。

468
00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:51.150
Does he like a pun card?
他喜欢双关语卡片吗？

469
00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.270
He loves a pun.
他超爱双关语。

470
00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.570
He's a punner.
他是个双关语达人。

471
00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:54.870
There's one in every family.
每个家庭里都有这么一个人。

472
00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:55.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

473
00:19:55.750 --> 00:20:00.170
I am not the punner, but somehow I still get cards with puns.
我不是那种爱玩双关语的人，但不知怎么的，我还是会收到双关语卡片。

474
00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:05.970
I got one one time from a friend of mine that it was just a picture of a sofa, and it said,
有一次我朋友送我一张，上面就画着一张沙发，写着，

475
00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:07.690
you're Sofa King Awesome.
你真是“沙发”王（Sofa King）棒极了。

476
00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.050
It took me a second.
我反应了一会儿才明白。

477
00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:14.530
Clever.
真聪明。

478
00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:19.370
Well, Jim is going to question whether or not Stanley has a mustache.
嗯，吉姆开始质疑斯坦利到底有没有胡子。

479
00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:19.970
Yeah.
是啊。

480
00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:24.330
And everyone's like, no, he does have a mustache.
然后大家都说，不，他确实有胡子。

481
00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.270
Well, some people feel very strongly that he does.
嗯，有些人非常坚定地认为他有。

482
00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.530
Some people feel like, no way, he does not.
有些人觉得，不可能，他绝对没有。

483
00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.970
And then some people are waffling.
还有些人摇摆不定。

484
00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.610
I did break it down.
我确实做过统计。

485
00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:35.250
Here's how the Dunder Mifflin Bunch voted by show of hands.
以下是邓德·米夫林员工举手表决的结果。

486
00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.630
Team Stash are Pam, Dwight, Creed, and Oscar.
“有胡子派”是帕姆、德怀特、克里德和奥斯卡。

487
00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:42.150
Team No Stash, Jim, Phyllis, Angela.
“没胡子派”是吉姆、菲利斯、安吉拉。

488
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.090
Team Unsure About the Stash, Kevin.
“不确定派”是凯文。

489
00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.670
I feel like Phyllis raises both hands.
我觉得菲利斯两只手都举起来了。

490
00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.970
She has two hands up at the end.
最后她两只手都举着。

491
00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:50.970
Yes, that's true.
是的，没错。

492
00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.450
She might be unsure.
她可能是不确定。

493
00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:54.410
She might be in Team Unsure Stash.
她可能属于“不确定派”。

494
00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.310
I mean, Pam even draws a picture.
我是说，帕姆甚至还画了画。

495
00:20:56.310 --> 00:21:00.430
She draws a mustache Stanley and a no mustache Stanley.
她画了一个有胡子的斯坦利和一个没胡子的斯坦利。

496
00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:02.210
That didn't seem to help.
那似乎没什么帮助。

497
00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:05.050
But we did get a lot of mail about these drawings.
但我们确实收到了很多关于这些画的来信。

498
00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:05.990
Jocelyn V.
来自犹他州圣乔治的乔斯林·V，

499
00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:08.130
in St. George, Utah, Millie P.
来自北卡罗来纳州达勒姆的米莉·P，

500
00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.330
from Durham, North Carolina, and Zoe G.
还有佐伊·G。

501
00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:11.790
from Irvine, California,
来自加利福尼亚州尔湾市，

502
00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:17.910
all said, Jenna, in the cold open when everyone is trying to remember whether or not Stanley has a mustache,
总而言之，珍娜，在那个冷开场里，大家都在努力回忆斯坦利到底有没有留胡子，

503
00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.030
Pam draws two pictures of Stanley in eight seconds.
帕姆在八秒钟内画了两张斯坦利的画像。

504
00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.190
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

505
00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:32.690
At 50 seconds, she is standing next to Phyllis, and at 58, she says okay and then holds up two full-page recognizable sketches of Stanley.
在50秒时，她站在菲利斯旁边，到了58秒，她说“好吧”，然后举起了两张画满整页、清晰可辨的斯坦利素描。

506
00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:40.290
In re-watching the scene, Pam's frantic faux-speed sketching in the background of Jim's line had me cracking up.
重看这一幕时，帕姆在吉姆台词背景下那种疯狂的假装速写让我笑得前仰后合。

507
00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:43.690
That means she only had four seconds for each of those pictures.
这意味着她每张画只有四秒钟的时间。

508
00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.070
Who really drew those pictures?
那些画到底是谁画的？

509
00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:48.790
Were you directed to draw really fast?
你们当时有被要求画得特别快吗？

510
00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:52.050
Please tell us everything you remember about this scene.
请告诉我们关于这一幕你还记得的一切。

511
00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.410
Well, Jocelyn, Millie, and Zoe, I have a curveball to throw at you.
好吧，乔斯琳、米莉和佐伊，我要给你们抛出一个难题。

512
00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:01.830
What if Pam has sketched everyone in the office and keeps them in her desk drawer?
如果帕姆其实把办公室里的每个人都画了一遍，并把画藏在办公桌抽屉里呢？

513
00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.350
That sounds like something Dwight would do.
听起来像是德怀特会做的事。

514
00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:05.670
I know.
我知道。

515
00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:08.510
Because he's going to need a wanted poster at any moment.
因为他随时都可能需要一张通缉令。

516
00:22:08.610 --> 00:22:09.630
But Pam has drawn Dwight.
但帕姆确实画过德怀特。

517
00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:10.910
This is true.
这倒是真的。

518
00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.030
Well, first of all, I did not draw those pictures.
好吧，首先，那些画不是我画的。

519
00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:15.410
They were pre-set for me.
它们是提前准备好的。

520
00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:18.330
I'm pretending to draw feverishly.
我只是在假装疯狂地作画。

521
00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:22.490
But there were a few lines of dialogue in the scene that got cut out.
但那一幕里有几句台词被剪掉了。

522
00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:26.790
The original script allowed me more time to draw these pictures.
原剧本给了我更多时间来画这些画。

523
00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:33.790
So in the scene, Pam says, Phyllis would know if Stanley has a mustache.
所以在那一幕里，帕姆说，菲利斯应该知道斯坦利有没有留胡子。

524
00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.370
She sits across from him every day.
她每天都坐在他对面。

525
00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:37.490
And Phyllis is like, oh, my God, I don't know.
然后菲利斯说，天哪，我不知道。

526
00:22:37.590 --> 00:22:38.830
Now I think he doesn't.
现在我觉得他没留。

527
00:22:38.950 --> 00:22:40.930
And Pam says, oh, come on, Phyllis.
帕姆说，噢，拜托，菲利斯。

528
00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:42.590
The whole card depends on this.
整张卡片的内容全指望这个了。

529
00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:45.850
So at this point, Jim would have thrown to Kevin.
所以在那一点上，吉姆本该把话题抛给凯文。

530
00:22:46.250 --> 00:22:49.450
He would have said, Kevin, does Stanley have a mustache?
他本该说，凯文，斯坦利有留胡子吗？

531
00:22:50.110 --> 00:22:53.310
And Kevin would have said, OK, I'm picturing him.
然后凯文会说，好吧，我在脑海里想象他。

532
00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:56.210
Now I'm asking him if he has a mustache.
现在我在问他有没有留胡子。

533
00:22:57.350 --> 00:22:58.770
He's not answering, guys.
伙计们，他不回答我。

534
00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:06.270
And also, Creed would have said, when I close my eyes, I see a mustache and a white beard
而且，克里德本该说，当我闭上眼睛，我看到了一撇胡子和白色的长胡须，

535
00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:07.870
and a red suit.
还有一身红色的套装。

536
00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:09.550
He's my father.
他是我父亲。

537
00:23:09.550 --> 00:23:12.050
And he's asking me to guide his sleigh tonight.
他正请求我今晚为他的雪橇指路。

538
00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:15.130
Don't ask Creed ever.
永远别问克里德。

539
00:23:16.030 --> 00:23:17.010
Don't ask Creed.
别问克里德。

540
00:23:17.270 --> 00:23:22.770
The script did say that I was supposed to hold up two, quote, hastily made drawings.
剧本确实写着我应该举起两张“匆忙完成的”画作。

541
00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:31.370
It also noted that the one with the mustache should be a giant mustache, not an accurate mustache.
上面还注明了有胡子的那张应该画个巨大的胡子，而不是准确的胡子。

542
00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:33.170
So there you have it.
所以事情就是这样。

543
00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:33.990
That's what happened.
这就是当时的情况。

544
00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:37.650
I had more time, but they kind of snipped some of it away.
我本来有更多时间，但他们把其中一部分剪掉了。

545
00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:42.650
You had more time, but still not enough to do those two drawings, in my opinion.
你确实有更多时间，但在我看来，还是不足以完成那两幅画。

546
00:23:42.790 --> 00:23:43.310
But that's OK.
不过没关系。

547
00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:44.550
It's a little bit of TV magic.
这就是一点电视魔法。

548
00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:46.590
I feel like it would have doubled my time.
我觉得那本来能让我的时间翻倍。

549
00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:48.830
Do you think 16 seconds is enough time?
你觉得16秒够吗？

550
00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:49.910
It might have been more.
可能还不止。

551
00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:52.490
Because, you know, Kevin does a whole visualization thing.
因为，你知道的，凯文做了一整套可视化演示。

552
00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:53.710
I don't know.
我不知道。

553
00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:58.850
Well, I guess it depends on your skill set, because I would have needed all day to do that.
嗯，我想这取决于你的技能水平，因为我得花上一整天才能做到那样。

554
00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:03.170
Well, Gabe is very excited because Stanley is arriving.
嗯，盖博非常兴奋，因为斯坦利要到了。

555
00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:08.450
And as Stanley walks in, Gabe covers his face so we can't see.
当斯坦利走进来时，盖博遮住了他的脸，这样我们就看不到了。

556
00:24:08.450 --> 00:24:12.590
And then does sort of a, like, ta-da, and he does, in fact, have a mustache.
然后他做了一个类似“当当”的动作，事实上，他确实留了胡子。

557
00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:15.570
We got a fan question from Veronica R.
我们收到了来自伊利诺伊州帕克城的维罗妮卡·R发来的粉丝提问，

558
00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:17.330
in Park City, Illinois, who said,
她说，

559
00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:21.330
where did the idea of Stanley having or not having a mustache come from?
斯坦利到底有没有胡子这个想法是从哪儿来的？

560
00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:26.210
Was this based on a real conversation about whether or not Leslie had a mustache?
这是基于关于莱斯利是否留胡子的真实讨论吗？

561
00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:30.530
Well, Veronica, we got to trade some messages with our writer, Steve Healy.
嗯，维罗妮卡，我们和我们的编剧史蒂夫·希利交流了一些信息。

562
00:24:30.970 --> 00:24:33.870
And he said that this idea came up in the writer's room.
他说这个想法是在编剧室里提出来的。

563
00:24:33.870 --> 00:24:38.670
He said it was either Mindy or BJ who pointed out that it was really hard to visualize
他说，是敏迪还是BJ指出，真的很难想象

564
00:24:38.670 --> 00:24:41.330
whether or not Leslie had a mustache or not.
莱斯利到底有没有留胡子。

565
00:24:41.510 --> 00:24:43.930
He said that the writer's room did have a debate,
他说编剧室确实进行了一场辩论，

566
00:24:43.930 --> 00:24:48.750
and only about 85% felt 100% sure he had one.
只有大约85%的人百分之百确定他留了胡子。

567
00:24:49.170 --> 00:24:52.130
I thought this was so relatable when Steve shared this with us,
当史蒂夫和我们分享这一点时，我觉得太有共鸣了，

568
00:24:52.130 --> 00:24:56.130
because how many times are you sitting around, like, at dinner with friends
因为有多少次你和认识很久的朋友坐在一起吃晚饭，

569
00:24:56.130 --> 00:24:58.650
that you've known forever, and someone's like,
然后有人说，

570
00:24:58.750 --> 00:25:00.870
oh, yeah, you know, Jenna has blue eyes.
哦，对，你知道的，珍娜有双蓝眼睛。

571
00:25:00.950 --> 00:25:02.090
And they're like, no, she doesn't.
然后他们说，不，她没有。

572
00:25:02.210 --> 00:25:03.570
Like, what are you talking about?
就像，你在说什么呢？

573
00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:04.630
She has blue eyes.
她就是有双蓝眼睛。

574
00:25:04.710 --> 00:25:05.950
And then that whole debate starts.
然后整场辩论就开始了。

575
00:25:06.090 --> 00:25:07.930
Like, no, it happens.
真的，这种情况确实会发生。

576
00:25:08.510 --> 00:25:10.270
When I was watching the cold open.
当我在看开场戏的时候。

577
00:25:10.630 --> 00:25:11.990
Did it make you second guess?
它让你产生怀疑了吗？

578
00:25:12.190 --> 00:25:12.610
It did.
确实有。

579
00:25:12.690 --> 00:25:13.050
Me too.
我也是。

580
00:25:13.230 --> 00:25:14.470
I was not sure.
我不确定了。

581
00:25:14.810 --> 00:25:15.990
I was like, wait, no, he does.
我当时想，等等，不，他有。

582
00:25:16.090 --> 00:25:16.510
He does.
他有。

583
00:25:16.730 --> 00:25:16.850
Doesn't he?
他没有吗？

584
00:25:17.310 --> 00:25:18.010
He does.
他有。

585
00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:18.850
Yes.
是的。

586
00:25:19.230 --> 00:25:22.790
But you just plant that seed of doubt, and then you aren't sure.
但你只要种下怀疑的种子，你就没法确定了。

587
00:25:22.990 --> 00:25:23.230
Yeah.
是啊。

588
00:25:24.290 --> 00:25:25.770
Well, Steve was so gracious.
嗯，史蒂夫非常客气。

589
00:25:25.770 --> 00:25:28.930
We reached out to him with a few questions, and we're going to sprinkle those in.
我们向他提了几个问题，我们会在节目中穿插这些内容。

590
00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:32.010
Well, I've got something to share from him right off the top.
嗯，我一开始就有些东西要分享。

591
00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:37.130
After the opening credits, we got a fan mail flurry again about Nellie not being featured
片头字幕之后，我们又收到了一大波粉丝来信，询问为什么奈莉没有作为经理出现。

592
00:25:37.130 --> 00:25:37.950
as the manager.
是的，我也注意到了。

593
00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:40.010
Yes, I noticed that, too.
我本以为这次的片头字幕肯定会有她坐在办公桌前的镜头，但并没有。

594
00:25:40.110 --> 00:25:46.210
I thought for sure this opening credits would have something with her on her desk, but no.
我问了史蒂夫·希利这件事。

595
00:25:46.210 --> 00:25:47.910
I asked Steve Healy about it.
我说，编剧们对奈莉担任经理有什么剧情规划吗？

596
00:25:48.010 --> 00:25:51.390
I said, did the writers have an arc in mind for Nellie as manager?
他说并没有明确的计划。

597
00:25:52.150 --> 00:25:54.810
And he said there was not a clear plan.
对于其他经理，这算是预先计划好的。

598
00:25:55.130 --> 00:25:58.970
With the other managers, it was sort of pre-planned.
他们知道那会是一个完整的剧情线。

599
00:25:59.150 --> 00:26:00.890
They knew it was going to be an arc.
他说，在这一点上，他们基本上是写一周算一周。

600
00:26:01.110 --> 00:26:04.450
He said they were kind of, at this point, writing week to week.
他说，在这一点上，他们基本上是写一周算一周。

601
00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:05.370
Oh, geez.
噢，天哪。

602
00:26:05.710 --> 00:26:05.890
Yeah.
是啊。

603
00:26:06.150 --> 00:26:06.970
Oh, my gosh.
天呐。

604
00:26:06.970 --> 00:26:12.810
He said he did remember talking to Catherine Tate one day at lunch early on, and she had
他说他确实记得早些时候有一天午餐时和凯瑟琳·塔特聊过，她当时

605
00:26:12.810 --> 00:26:15.990
shared that she found California kind of odd compared to London.
分享说她觉得加州和伦敦比起来有点奇怪。

606
00:26:16.370 --> 00:26:21.530
So they did try to incorporate some of that kind of fish-out-of-water stuff into her character.
所以他们确实尝试把那种“初来乍到”的感觉融入到她的角色中。

607
00:26:21.610 --> 00:26:25.510
So that was something that they had pre-planned for her arrival to Scranton.
所以那是他们为她来到斯克兰顿预先计划好的。

608
00:26:25.650 --> 00:26:29.990
But they didn't know about Nellie's position within the Dunder Mifflin hierarchy.
但他们当时并不清楚奈莉在邓德·米夫林公司层级中的位置。

609
00:26:30.450 --> 00:26:32.450
Or how long she would be staying manager.
也不知道她会担任经理多久。

610
00:26:32.450 --> 00:26:35.450
They were kind of deciding week to week how that would go.
他们当时基本上是走一步看一步，决定剧情走向。

611
00:26:35.450 --> 00:26:36.430
Oh, got it.
噢，明白了。

612
00:26:36.770 --> 00:26:40.850
Well, Robert California is going to arrive, and he's not greeted by anyone because Aaron
好吧，罗伯特·加州即将登场，但他没受到任何人的欢迎，因为亚伦

613
00:26:40.850 --> 00:26:41.510
is in Florida.
在佛罗里达。

614
00:26:42.050 --> 00:26:45.690
He sneaks up behind Pam, who has headphones on.
他悄悄走到戴着耳机的帕姆身后。

615
00:26:46.070 --> 00:26:47.430
She's drinking her coffee.
她正在喝咖啡。

616
00:26:47.690 --> 00:26:48.710
She's rocking out.
她正在跟着音乐摇摆。

617
00:26:49.410 --> 00:26:53.610
Yeah, she is listening to Drake featuring Swizz Beats.
没错，她当时在听德雷克和史威兹·毕兹合作的歌。

618
00:26:54.570 --> 00:26:56.390
I have an audio clip.
我有一段音频剪辑。

619
00:26:56.710 --> 00:27:00.070
Would you like to hear what Pam was warming up with for the day?
你想听听帕姆那天早上是用什么来热身的吗？

620
00:27:00.290 --> 00:27:02.770
Oh, I know what she was warming up to, but I think we should all hear it.
噢，我知道她在听什么热身，但我认为我们都应该听听。

621
00:27:02.810 --> 00:27:03.770
It's fancy.
这很时髦。

622
00:27:04.010 --> 00:27:04.670
Oh, I know.
噢，我知道。

623
00:27:25.620 --> 00:27:26.180
All right.
好吧。

624
00:27:26.360 --> 00:27:28.800
