942
00:40:09.780 --> 00:40:12.520
St. Louis catch at 4 minutes and 41 seconds.
菲利斯提议点一些胡萝卜蛋糕。

943
00:40:13.580 --> 00:40:16.760
Phyllis proposes the idea of ordering some carrot cake.
点（Arder）。

944
00:40:17.060 --> 00:40:17.400
Arder.
这和爆米花那段如出一辙，那可是个大订单。

945
00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:21.760
It falls right in line with popcorn and that's a big order.
她是这么说的。

946
00:40:22.740 --> 00:40:23.420
She does.
她想“点（art）”一些胡萝卜蛋糕。

947
00:40:23.420 --> 00:40:25.700
She wants to art her some carrot cake.
这就是我的发现。

948
00:40:26.400 --> 00:40:27.300
Those are my catches.
每次你们发现菲利斯带出圣路易斯口音，都是我最喜欢的事情之一。

949
00:40:27.900 --> 00:40:32.360
Every time you guys catch Phyllis having a St. Louis accent is one of my favorite things.
我同意。

950
00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:33.180
I agree.
我同意。

951
00:40:33.700 --> 00:40:37.220
Well, lady, let's take a break because when we get back, we're going to be hauling cube.
好了，女士，我们休息一下，因为回来之后，我们要开始大干一场了。

952
00:40:37.620 --> 00:40:38.880
Yeah, we should rest up.
没错，我们是该休息一下。

953
00:40:51.680 --> 00:40:52.660
We are back.
我们回来了。

954
00:40:52.660 --> 00:40:57.880
And before we haul some cube, Andy and Erin are going to do some breakup scenarios in the
在开始大干一场之前，安迪和艾琳要在车里进行一些分手演练。

955
00:40:57.880 --> 00:40:58.220
car.
车里。

956
00:40:58.360 --> 00:40:59.260
Get a little role play.
来点角色扮演。

957
00:40:59.960 --> 00:41:02.000
We had a fan question from Mallory C.
我们收到了来自北卡罗来纳州达勒姆市马洛里·C的一位粉丝提问，她说，

958
00:41:02.240 --> 00:41:04.500
in Durham, North Carolina, who said,
在安迪和艾琳为安迪与杰西卡的分手做练习的那场戏里，看起来

959
00:41:04.500 --> 00:41:09.840
in the scene where Andy and Erin are practicing for Andy's breakup with Jessica, it looks like
当艾莉说“怎么了？”的时候，艾德笑场了，那是真笑。

960
00:41:09.840 --> 00:41:14.320
Ed broke and genuinely laughed when Ellie said, what is it?
我昨晚没睡好。

961
00:41:14.380 --> 00:41:15.800
I didn't sleep well last night.
那是剧本里写的吗？

962
00:41:16.300 --> 00:41:17.600
Was that scripted?
马洛里，那不是。

963
00:41:18.540 --> 00:41:19.580
Mallory, it was not.
那是即兴发挥的。

964
00:41:19.940 --> 00:41:21.400
It was improvised.
我想他们当时就是让他们自由发挥。

965
00:41:22.040 --> 00:41:23.880
I think they just let them go.
百分之百是让他们自由发挥。

966
00:41:24.100 --> 00:41:26.140
They 100% just let them go.
如果你想知道我们是在哪里拍摄驾驶场景的，不用再猜了。

967
00:41:26.440 --> 00:41:31.260
If you are wondering where we shot the driving scenes, wonder no more.
首先，艾德并没有在开车。

968
00:41:31.260 --> 00:41:33.300
First of all, Ed was not driving.
我们用拖车架把车固定住，然后由一辆拍摄专用车牵引。

969
00:41:33.960 --> 00:41:38.320
We hooked up the car to a dolly and it was pulled by an insert car.
那是行话，就像平板卡车一样。

970
00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:41.580
That's lingo for like a flatbed truck.
在卡车后面，坐着我们所有的工作人员。

971
00:41:41.920 --> 00:41:44.920
And in the back of the truck, we have all our crew.
有摄像、录音、导演、副导演。

972
00:41:45.040 --> 00:41:47.300
We have camera, sound, director, assistant director.
我爸爸以前有一辆平板卡车。

973
00:41:47.680 --> 00:41:49.320
My dad had a flatbed truck.
他有没有拖过拍摄用车？

974
00:41:49.540 --> 00:41:51.940
Did he ever pull a picture car?
那是行话，指演员坐在里面的那辆车。

975
00:41:52.120 --> 00:41:55.340
That's lingo for the car the actors are in.
他拖过很多马车拖车、农用设备，但他还装了一堆我的东西，

976
00:41:55.340 --> 00:42:01.560
He pulled a lot of horse trailer, farming equipment, but he also loaded up a bunch of my stuff and
开着那辆平板卡车，后面还挂着一个拖车。

977
00:42:01.560 --> 00:42:05.140
drove the flatbed truck with a trailer attached to it.
我就是那样搬到洛杉矶的。

978
00:42:05.200 --> 00:42:06.460
And that's how I moved to LA.
你带了多少东西？

979
00:42:07.260 --> 00:42:09.160
How much stuff did you take?
你把东西放在平板卡车上，后面还挂了个拖车？

980
00:42:09.380 --> 00:42:12.640
You had stuff in the flatbed and in a trailer behind it?
那辆平板卡车很小，很短，但他还挂了一个加长拖车。

981
00:42:12.640 --> 00:42:16.860
The flatbed truck is pretty small, pretty short, but he also had an extended trailer
他会把它连上去。

982
00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:17.960
he would attach to it.
但我搬来的时候只带了一个手提箱，我就靠那个箱子过活。

983
00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:22.300
But I moved here with just a suitcase and I lived out of a suitcase.
最后，我妈说：“比尔，装车。”

984
00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:24.960
And then finally, my mom was like, Bill, load up.
我们要给她带些家具过去。

985
00:42:25.100 --> 00:42:26.220
We're going to bring her some furniture.
噢，那真是太好了。

986
00:42:26.640 --> 00:42:28.180
Oh, that was really nice.
我知道。

987
00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:28.620
I know.
嗯，那辆平板卡车很大。

988
00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:30.700
Well, this flatbed was large.
我有一张它的照片。

989
00:42:30.700 --> 00:42:31.820
I have a picture of it.
我们有了平板卡车。

990
00:42:32.120 --> 00:42:33.520
We got the flatbed truck.
我们把车固定在上面。

991
00:42:33.520 --> 00:42:35.120
We've attached a car to it.
我们还有一群精密驾驶员，他们会绕着拍摄用车行驶，这样一切

992
00:42:35.280 --> 00:42:41.580
We also had a bunch of precision drivers who drive around the picture car so that everything
都能保持高度一致。

993
00:42:41.580 --> 00:42:42.880
stays really consistent.
你会注意到这些车行驶的速度几乎完全一样。

994
00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:46.780
You'll notice the cars drive sort of at the exact same speed.
确实，超车的情况并不多。

995
00:42:46.780 --> 00:42:48.220
Indeed, there's not a lot of passing.
史蒂夫·希利说，拍摄所有这些驾驶场景比他预想的要复杂得多，

996
00:42:49.260 --> 00:42:53.160
Steve Healy said that getting all these driving scenes was way more complicated than he realized
因为他当时就在片场。

997
00:42:53.160 --> 00:42:54.480
because he was on set.
编剧总是会出现在他们负责的那集拍摄现场。

998
00:42:54.600 --> 00:42:56.800
The writer would always be on set for their episode.
它们总是更复杂。

999
00:42:56.820 --> 00:42:57.960
They were always more complicated.
总是更复杂。

1000
00:42:58.160 --> 00:42:59.160
Always more complicated.
总是更复杂。

1001
00:42:59.160 --> 00:43:00.560
It's a lot of moving parts.
这涉及很多变动环节。

1002
00:43:00.960 --> 00:43:03.220
And we shot this all on a real highway.
而且我们是在真正的公路上拍摄的。

1003
00:43:03.920 --> 00:43:06.040
I mean, I guess, obviously, right?
我是说，我想这显而易见，对吧？

1004
00:43:06.120 --> 00:43:07.000
We didn't build a highway.
我们没去建一条公路。

1005
00:43:07.380 --> 00:43:08.820
That should have gone without saying.
这本该是不言而喻的。

1006
00:43:09.400 --> 00:43:10.440
We've done it before.
我们以前做过。

1007
00:43:10.900 --> 00:43:12.840
We did it for Pam and Jim's engagement.
为了帕姆和吉姆的订婚我们做过。

1008
00:43:12.960 --> 00:43:14.480
But we did not do it this time.
但这次我们没这么做。

1009
00:43:14.600 --> 00:43:14.840
No.
没有。

1010
00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:15.600
Real road.
真正的公路。

1011
00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:18.240
Now, everyone, we're going to haul some cube.
好了各位，我们要全速前进（haul some cube）了。

1012
00:43:18.480 --> 00:43:19.120
Thank God.
谢天谢地。

1013
00:43:19.120 --> 00:43:20.720
I've been waiting to haul cube.
我一直等着全速前进呢。

1014
00:43:21.340 --> 00:43:22.640
I love this expression.
我喜欢这个表达。

1015
00:43:22.720 --> 00:43:24.120
I want to start saying it.
我想开始用这个词了。

1016
00:43:24.280 --> 00:43:25.340
I'm hauling cube.
我要全速前进。

1017
00:43:25.540 --> 00:43:27.800
Every time I move from now on, I'm going to haul cube.
从现在开始，每次我移动，我都要说我要全速前进。

1018
00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:28.540
I'm going to haul cube.
我要全速前进。

1019
00:43:28.540 --> 00:43:36.360
How much stuff has Nellie brought with her from Florida?
奈莉从佛罗里达带了多少东西过来？

1020
00:43:36.720 --> 00:43:37.160
I know.
我知道。

1021
00:43:37.720 --> 00:43:39.300
And it's just now arriving.
而且现在才刚到。

1022
00:43:39.380 --> 00:43:40.060
A lot.
很多。

1023
00:43:40.160 --> 00:43:41.180
She's unpacked nothing.
她什么都没拆包。

1024
00:43:41.980 --> 00:43:43.340
I just want to point out.
我只想指出一点。

1025
00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:45.200
I don't feel like she's ever going to unpack.
我觉得她永远都不会拆包了。

1026
00:43:45.400 --> 00:43:46.320
I'm just going to say this.
我只想说这个。

1027
00:43:46.420 --> 00:43:50.520
I think that Nellie just brings a bunch of boxes and one big comfy chair, and that's it.
我觉得奈莉就是带了一堆箱子和一把大大的舒适椅子，就这样。

1028
00:43:50.660 --> 00:43:52.760
She just digs in a box when she needs something.
她需要什么的时候就从箱子里翻。

1029
00:43:52.760 --> 00:43:53.720
That's possible.
有可能。

1030
00:43:54.380 --> 00:44:00.060
Nellie's apartment was in a real apartment complex on Wilkerson Avenue in Valley Village.
奈莉的公寓位于谷村威尔克森大道的一个真实公寓区。

1031
00:44:00.360 --> 00:44:01.900
We did not build this set.
我们没有搭建这个布景。

1032
00:44:02.080 --> 00:44:03.600
We went on location for this.
我们是去实地拍摄的。

1033
00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:08.540
As Jim and Dwight help Nellie, they're really struggling with one of her big oversized chairs.
当吉姆和德怀特帮奈莉搬家时，他们正费力地搬她那把超大号椅子。

1034
00:44:08.820 --> 00:44:09.920
Dwight says, you know what?
德怀特说，你知道吗？

1035
00:44:10.020 --> 00:44:11.020
We'll work our magic.
我们会施展魔法的。

1036
00:44:11.220 --> 00:44:11.900
We'll make it fit.
我们会让它塞进去的。

1037
00:44:12.200 --> 00:44:13.180
Nellie's like, no, no, no.
奈莉说，不，不，不。

1038
00:44:13.320 --> 00:44:13.780
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1039
00:44:13.880 --> 00:44:15.040
No magicians.
不要魔术师。

1040
00:44:15.760 --> 00:44:16.920
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1041
00:44:17.020 --> 00:44:17.960
Let's not go there.
我们别提这个了。

1042
00:44:18.160 --> 00:44:19.880
Nothing is more repellent than magicians.
没有什么比魔术师更让人反感的了。

1043
00:44:20.060 --> 00:44:23.540
Bunch of grown men waving wands, pulling bunnies out of body crevices.
一群成年男人挥舞着魔杖，从身体缝隙里掏出兔子。

1044
00:44:23.940 --> 00:44:25.480
Magicians are repulsive.
魔术师真令人作呕。

1045
00:44:25.900 --> 00:44:26.520
Next topic.
下一个话题。

1046
00:44:27.300 --> 00:44:27.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1047
00:44:27.780 --> 00:44:29.820
This is a lot of information out of nowhere.
这突如其来的一大堆信息。

1048
00:44:30.740 --> 00:44:32.720
Super passionate amounts of information.
充满激情的各种信息。

1049
00:44:33.600 --> 00:44:36.140
That don't really apply to moving you into your apartment.
跟帮你搬进公寓根本没关系。

1050
00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:39.060
Well, Jim's going to use that information.
好吧，吉姆会用上这些信息的。

1051
00:44:39.240 --> 00:44:44.380
Pam's going to call him on the phone and tell him all about their hilarious bad party plan.
帕姆会打电话告诉他，关于他们那个滑稽又糟糕的派对计划的一切。

1052
00:44:45.000 --> 00:44:48.920
And Jim says, oh, hire a magician.
然后吉姆说，哦，雇个魔术师吧。

1053
00:44:49.140 --> 00:44:49.660
Trust me.
相信我。

1054
00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:50.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1055
00:44:50.600 --> 00:44:51.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1056
00:44:51.380 --> 00:44:56.840
Well, we asked Steve Healy if they had been planting a seed about this magician storyline with Nellie.
我们问了史蒂夫·希利，他们是否在奈莉的这条魔术师剧情线上埋下了伏笔。

1057
00:44:56.960 --> 00:45:02.780
Because remember, in last week's episode, when Nellie arrived in Scranton, she said she hated the Houdini Museum.
因为记得吗，在上周的剧集中，奈莉刚到斯克兰顿时，她说她讨厌胡迪尼博物馆。

1058
00:45:03.490 --> 00:45:04.620
I'm surprised she went.
我很惊讶她竟然去了。

1059
00:45:05.040 --> 00:45:06.620
I don't think she went.
我觉得她没去。

1060
00:45:06.700 --> 00:45:08.120
I think she just knows it's there.
我想她只是知道那里有这个地方。

1061
00:45:08.360 --> 00:45:08.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1062
00:45:08.960 --> 00:45:10.120
Here's what Steve said.
史蒂夫是这么说的。

1063
00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:15.240
Steve said he doesn't really remember that they were intentionally planning this whole magician storyline.
史蒂夫说他不记得他们当时是有意策划了整个魔术师剧情线。

1064
00:45:15.640 --> 00:45:20.340
But he said there is some natural tension between comedians and magicians.
但他提到喜剧演员和魔术师之间确实存在某种天然的张力。

1065
00:45:20.700 --> 00:45:25.100
Lots of comedy people start out as magicians or flirt with magic at some point.
很多喜剧人起初都是魔术师，或者在某个阶段接触过魔术。

1066
00:45:25.100 --> 00:45:30.460
And comedians are also such skeptics, they often get irrationally angry at magicians.
而且喜剧演员通常非常多疑，他们经常会对魔术师产生非理性的愤怒。

1067
00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:32.280
And that might have been part of it.
这可能也是原因之一。

1068
00:45:32.760 --> 00:45:37.220
Steve said, I remember some of the writers in those days were going to the Magic Castle.
史蒂夫说，我记得当时有些编剧会去魔术城堡。

1069
00:45:37.620 --> 00:45:40.300
Magic was a frequent topic in the room.
魔术是编剧室里经常讨论的话题。

1070
00:45:40.460 --> 00:45:41.640
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

1071
00:45:42.080 --> 00:45:43.260
That's very funny.
那太有趣了。

1072
00:45:43.440 --> 00:45:43.900
Isn't that?
不是吗？

1073
00:45:44.140 --> 00:45:47.020
Well, remember, I was a comedic magician.
好吧，记得吗，我以前是个喜剧魔术师。

1074
00:45:47.020 --> 00:45:51.540
I performed my comedic magic show at stand-up nights.
我曾在单口喜剧之夜表演过我的喜剧魔术秀。

1075
00:45:51.800 --> 00:45:53.680
I still want to bring that back.
我一直想把它重新捡起来。

1076
00:45:53.860 --> 00:45:55.540
I want to make it part of our live show.
我想把它加入到我们的现场演出中。

1077
00:45:55.720 --> 00:45:57.780
I want you to do your magic act.
我希望你表演你的魔术节目。

1078
00:45:57.980 --> 00:45:58.580
Of course.
当然。

1079
00:45:58.580 --> 00:46:00.260
Why have I not been doing it?
为什么我一直没做呢？

1080
00:46:00.260 --> 00:46:01.180
I don't know.
我不知道。

1081
00:46:01.960 --> 00:46:02.720
So, done.
那就这么定了。

1082
00:46:03.020 --> 00:46:03.400
Done.
定了。

1083
00:46:03.700 --> 00:46:06.240
I still have the cassette tape of music.
我还有那盘音乐磁带。

1084
00:46:06.240 --> 00:46:13.840
And I bought a, what do you call it, a tuxedo jacket with tails at a vintage shop.
而且我在一家复古店买了一件，怎么说呢，燕尾服外套。

1085
00:46:13.980 --> 00:46:14.120
Listen.
听着。

1086
00:46:14.120 --> 00:46:14.600
I have it.
我有那件衣服。

1087
00:46:14.600 --> 00:46:16.580
I know the perfect moment in our live show.
我知道在我们的现场演出中哪个时刻最合适。

1088
00:46:16.740 --> 00:46:17.720
I love our live show.
我爱我们的现场演出。

1089
00:46:17.920 --> 00:46:18.700
This has to happen.
这事儿必须成。

1090
00:46:18.700 --> 00:46:22.180
And I think I will be your assistant on roller skates.
我觉得我可以穿上旱冰鞋当你的助手。

1091
00:46:22.680 --> 00:46:25.400
I am so disappointed we are only just now thinking of it.
真遗憾我们现在才想到这一点。

1092
00:46:25.560 --> 00:46:26.960
But I am so happy that we did.
但我很高兴我们终于想到了。

1093
00:46:27.620 --> 00:46:28.920
We have to add it.
我们必须把它加进去。

1094
00:46:29.520 --> 00:46:33.380
Andy and Aaron are going to arrive now at Jessica's family cabin.
安迪和亚伦现在要到达杰西卡家的度假小屋了。

1095
00:46:33.580 --> 00:46:34.760
It is so charming.
那地方真迷人。

1096
00:46:35.700 --> 00:46:40.820
In the shooting draft, there was a scene where Aaron and Andy notice as they pull up that there
在拍摄剧本中，有一场戏是亚伦和安迪开车到达时注意到

1097
00:46:40.820 --> 00:46:42.480
seems to be a lot of people there.
那里似乎有很多人。

1098
00:46:42.660 --> 00:46:43.920
It read like this.
剧本是这样写的。

1099
00:46:44.440 --> 00:46:45.900
Exterior rural cabin.
外景，乡村小屋。

1100
00:46:46.300 --> 00:46:48.180
Andy and Aaron pull up to the cabin.
安迪和亚伦开车到达小屋。

1101
00:46:48.340 --> 00:46:49.640
There are several cars there.
那儿有几辆车。

1102
00:46:50.160 --> 00:46:52.980
Andy says, why are there so many cars here?
安迪问，为什么这儿有这么多车？

1103
00:46:53.340 --> 00:46:56.380
Aaron says, Jessica's parents must be rich.
亚伦说，杰西卡的父母一定很有钱。

1104
00:46:56.460 --> 00:46:57.200
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1105
00:46:57.280 --> 00:46:58.440
The cars aren't that nice.
那些车其实不怎么样。

1106
00:46:58.440 --> 00:47:03.000
Personally, I'd rather have two really nice cars than seven crappy ones.
就我个人而言，我宁愿要两辆真正的好车，也不要七辆破烂货。

1107
00:47:03.200 --> 00:47:04.620
Guess that's why I'm not rich.
我想这就是我为什么没钱的原因吧。

1108
00:47:04.980 --> 00:47:07.040
Andy says, this is weird.
安迪说，这太奇怪了。

1109
00:47:07.200 --> 00:47:09.220
And then there's a knock on their car window.
然后有人敲了他们的车窗。

1110
00:47:10.380 --> 00:47:15.740
Well, the knock on the window is from Lauren, played by Sue Redman.
敲窗户的人是劳伦，由苏·雷德曼饰演。

1111
00:47:15.940 --> 00:47:19.980
She studied acting at the Steppenwolf Theater in Chicago and studied improv at Second City,
她曾在芝加哥的荒原剧团学习表演，并在第二城喜剧团学习即兴表演，

1112
00:47:20.100 --> 00:47:20.460
Chicago.
就在芝加哥。

1113
00:47:21.480 --> 00:47:27.300
And according to IMDb, fun fact, she played a nurse in the movie Contagion and accidentally
根据IMDb上的趣闻，她在电影《传染病》中饰演一名护士，不小心

1114
00:47:27.300 --> 00:47:30.840
lodged a prop piece of medical equipment in Matt Damon's right ear.
把一个医疗道具塞进了马特·达蒙的右耳里。

1115
00:47:31.300 --> 00:47:32.620
How do you do that?
这怎么可能做到？

1116
00:47:32.920 --> 00:47:33.560
I don't know.
我不知道。

1117
00:47:33.740 --> 00:47:37.000
She misused the prop equipment, I suppose.
我想她是误用了那个道具吧。

1118
00:47:37.260 --> 00:47:38.620
She's giving him an exam.
她当时正在给他做检查。

1119
00:47:39.280 --> 00:47:41.220
And she lodged it in his ear?
然后就塞进他耳朵里了？

1120
00:47:41.460 --> 00:47:42.520
Yeah, I'm sure temporarily.
是啊，我肯定只是暂时的。

1121
00:47:43.620 --> 00:47:44.680
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1122
00:47:45.240 --> 00:47:45.880
You know what?
你知道吗？

1123
00:47:45.940 --> 00:47:49.280
This is exactly why I never, ever want to be on a medical show.
这就是为什么我永远、永远都不想去演医疗剧。

1124
00:47:49.920 --> 00:47:50.980
I would do that.
我肯定会干出那种事。

1125
00:47:50.980 --> 00:47:52.040
You might hurt somebody.
你可能会伤到人。

1126
00:47:52.180 --> 00:47:52.880
I don't know.
我不知道。

1127
00:47:53.500 --> 00:47:55.640
I just don't even know how you come back from that.
我甚至不知道出了这种事该怎么收场。

1128
00:47:55.840 --> 00:47:59.840
What is your end-of-the-day convo like after a day like that when you call your best friend?
如果发生这种事，你一天结束时给最好的朋友打电话，会怎么聊？

1129
00:48:00.020 --> 00:48:00.500
I don't know.
我不知道。

1130
00:48:00.600 --> 00:48:03.100
You're like, you would not believe what I did to Matt Damon today.
你会说，你绝对不敢相信我今天对马特·达蒙做了什么。

1131
00:48:03.760 --> 00:48:05.920
Yeah, that's how you would lead that convo.
没错，你肯定会这么开启话题。

1132
00:48:06.300 --> 00:48:06.980
For sure.
那肯定的。

1133
00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:10.280
Well, Lauren's going to tell them that Jessica is not there.
好了，劳伦要告诉他们杰西卡不在那儿。

1134
00:48:10.920 --> 00:48:12.420
She's gone for a jog.
她出去慢跑了。

1135
00:48:13.080 --> 00:48:19.440
This is right around the time when Aaron and Andy realize that they've come upon a bachelorette party.
就在这时，亚伦和安迪意识到他们闯进了一个单身派对。

1136
00:48:19.620 --> 00:48:20.780
She's wearing a veil.
她戴着面纱。

1137
00:48:20.980 --> 00:48:21.740
In her hair.
戴在头发上。

1138
00:48:21.940 --> 00:48:23.860
I would like to play a bullsh** card.
我想打出一张“胡扯”牌。

1139
00:48:24.340 --> 00:48:25.060
What is it?
怎么了？

1140
00:48:25.820 --> 00:48:27.500
Andy and Jessica are dating.
安迪和杰西卡在约会。

1141
00:48:27.820 --> 00:48:29.660
They're in a full-on relationship.
他们正在正式交往。

1142
00:48:29.920 --> 00:48:30.120
Right.
没错。

1143
00:48:30.440 --> 00:48:37.380
How is it that Andy wouldn't know that her good friend's getting married and they're going to be having this bachelorette thing at the cabin?
安迪怎么会不知道她好朋友要结婚，而且她们要在小屋举办单身派对呢？

1144
00:48:37.560 --> 00:48:37.860
How?
怎么会呢？

1145
00:48:38.060 --> 00:48:38.980
I hear you.
我明白你的意思。

1146
00:48:39.340 --> 00:48:42.780
You know, he knows she's at the cabin, but he doesn't know why.
你知道，他知道她在小屋，但他不知道原因。

1147
00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:44.120
She's just there solo.
他以为她只是独自在那儿。

1148
00:48:44.120 --> 00:48:45.800
Is he a bad listener?
他是个糟糕的倾听者吗？

1149
00:48:46.220 --> 00:48:50.620
You know, did Jessica say, hey, this weekend I'm going to be up at my parents' cabin.
你说，杰西卡有没有说过，嘿，这个周末我要去我父母的小屋。

1150
00:48:50.620 --> 00:48:52.180
My friend is, yeah.
我朋友在那儿，对。

1151
00:48:52.380 --> 00:48:53.740
I'm hosting the whole party.
这场派对由我全权负责。

1152
00:48:54.120 --> 00:48:54.900
It's kind of stressful.
压力还挺大的。

1153
00:48:55.100 --> 00:48:56.560
I have to buy extra groceries.
我得去多买些杂货。

1154
00:48:56.760 --> 00:48:58.260
Extra gummy penises.
多买些软糖丁丁。

1155
00:48:58.520 --> 00:48:59.300
Gummy penises.
软糖丁丁。

1156
00:48:59.420 --> 00:49:00.460
And a veil.
还有头纱。

1157
00:49:00.660 --> 00:49:02.700
And we have to have games.
而且我们还得准备游戏。

1158
00:49:02.700 --> 00:49:04.420
I'm going to blow up a bunch of balloons.
我打算吹一大堆气球。

1159
00:49:04.740 --> 00:49:05.860
Put people's names on them.
在上面写上大家的名字。

1160
00:49:05.900 --> 00:49:07.320
Tape it to a poster board.
贴在海报板上。

1161
00:49:07.320 --> 00:49:08.320
I'm very busy.
我忙得不可开交。

1162
00:49:08.560 --> 00:49:10.240
I mean, that's how I communicate with Lee.
我是说，这就是我和李沟通的方式。

1163
00:49:10.400 --> 00:49:11.440
He'd know all the deets.
他肯定知道所有细节。

1164
00:49:11.600 --> 00:49:12.560
He'd know everything.
他什么都知道。

1165
00:49:13.160 --> 00:49:19.300
We got a fan question from Santa M in Houston, Texas, who said, where was Jessica's cabin actually located?
我们收到了一位来自德克萨斯州休斯顿的粉丝Santa M的提问，她问：杰西卡的木屋实际上是在哪里拍摄的？

1166
00:49:19.300 --> 00:49:21.540
It looks a lot like East Coast cabins.
看起来很像东海岸的木屋。

1167
00:49:21.540 --> 00:49:23.100
Well, I'll tell you.
好吧，我来告诉你。

1168
00:49:23.220 --> 00:49:26.240
We shot this at a filming location called Canyon Ranch.
我们是在一个叫峡谷牧场的拍摄地拍的。

1169
00:49:26.240 --> 00:49:28.200
It is in the Santa Monica Mountains.
它位于圣莫尼卡山脉。

1170
00:49:28.900 --> 00:49:30.920
It's just a film location.
那只是个拍摄场地。

1171
00:49:31.220 --> 00:49:36.540
They have tons of different cabins and houses, and they have a fake gas station and a fake saloon.
那里有很多不同的木屋和房子，还有一个假加油站和一个假酒吧。

1172
00:49:36.980 --> 00:49:38.760
I looked all over the website.
我把他们的网站翻了个遍。

1173
00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:41.320
The cabin we used was fully decorated.
我们用的那个木屋是全装修好的。

1174
00:49:41.320 --> 00:49:43.640
If you go to the website, it looks exactly the same.
如果你去网站上看，它看起来一模一样。

1175
00:49:44.260 --> 00:49:49.380
This location has been used for all kinds of films and commercials, a lot of car commercials.
这个场地被用于各种电影和广告拍摄，尤其是很多汽车广告。

1176
00:49:49.720 --> 00:49:50.940
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

1177
00:49:51.480 --> 00:49:53.380
Has it been used for a horror movie?
它被用来拍过恐怖片吗？

1178
00:49:53.480 --> 00:49:57.420
Because I always feel like places with lots of cabins are where all the shit goes down.
因为我总觉得那种有很多木屋的地方，就是所有倒霉事发生的地方。

1179
00:49:57.540 --> 00:49:58.060
I am sure.
我敢肯定拍过。

1180
00:49:58.280 --> 00:50:01.480
But if you go to the website, they have a lot of rugged terrain.
但如果你去网站上看，他们有很多崎岖的地形。

1181
00:50:02.300 --> 00:50:08.100
So, you know, the shot of people, like, driving off-road to set up camp at a creek?
所以，你知道，那种人们开车越野去小溪边露营的镜头？

1182
00:50:08.280 --> 00:50:08.540
Yeah.
对。

1183
00:50:08.760 --> 00:50:09.480
Canyon Ranch.
峡谷牧场。

1184
00:50:09.640 --> 00:50:10.080
Got it.
明白了。

1185
00:50:10.420 --> 00:50:10.640
Yeah.
没错。

1186
00:50:10.760 --> 00:50:12.260
I saw a lot of those on the website.
我在网站上看到很多那样的场景。

1187
00:50:12.260 --> 00:50:15.160
I didn't see any horror movies, but I'm sure.
我没看到有恐怖片，但我敢肯定有。

1188
00:50:15.420 --> 00:50:15.800
Right?
是吧？

1189
00:50:16.140 --> 00:50:18.440
I wonder if Cabin in the Woods was shot there.
我在想《林中小屋》是不是在那儿拍的。

1190
00:50:18.880 --> 00:50:19.760
We'll never know.
我们永远也不会知道了。

1191
00:50:19.800 --> 00:50:20.480
We'll never know.
我们永远也不会知道了。

1192
00:50:20.660 --> 00:50:21.880
Mom Detective moment.
“妈妈侦探”时刻。

1193
00:50:22.020 --> 00:50:22.640
We'll never know.
我们永远也不会知道了。

1194
00:50:23.180 --> 00:50:28.080
Well, Steve Healy said that the cabin they filmed at had some really kooky angles.
史蒂夫·希利说他们拍摄的那个木屋有一些非常古怪的角度。

1195
00:50:28.340 --> 00:50:28.740
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

1196
00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:31.360
And it was very challenging to get some of the shots.
要拍到某些镜头非常有挑战性。

1197
00:50:31.560 --> 00:50:35.680
He also said that he didn't think the Santa Monica Mountains looked much like Pennsylvania,
他还说他觉得圣莫尼卡山脉看起来不太像宾夕法尼亚州，

1198
00:50:35.680 --> 00:50:39.680
but our writer Danny Chun is from that area and vouched for it.
但我们的编剧丹尼·春就是那个地方的人，他为它背书了。

1199
00:50:39.960 --> 00:50:41.300
I thought it looked authentic.
我觉得看起来挺真实的。

1200
00:50:41.960 --> 00:50:48.460
And the fact that the cabin came fully furnished probably means that we didn't move stuff around,
而且木屋自带全套家具，可能意味着我们没怎么挪动过里面的东西，

1201
00:50:48.480 --> 00:50:50.500
which was challenging for us.
这对我们来说很有挑战性。

1202
00:50:50.680 --> 00:50:50.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1203
00:50:51.100 --> 00:50:51.840
I see that.
我明白了。

1204
00:50:52.220 --> 00:50:57.740
Back to Nellie's apartment, Dwight is unpacking things, and he wonders out loud if king-size
回到内莉的公寓，德怀特正在拆东西，他大声琢磨着在英国特大号床单是不是叫总统号，

1205
00:50:57.740 --> 00:51:02.280
sheets are called presidential in England, and he really wishes he had a tweeter account.
他真希望自己有个推特账号。

1206
00:51:03.040 --> 00:51:06.720
Let me tell you what happened to me after this comment.
让我告诉你在这条评论之后我发生了什么。

1207
00:51:07.140 --> 00:51:07.780
Let me guess.
让我猜猜。

1208
00:51:07.900 --> 00:51:11.620
Something to do with either bedding or tweeter.
跟床上用品或者推特有关？

1209
00:51:12.300 --> 00:51:12.860
Bedding.
床上用品。

1210
00:51:13.100 --> 00:51:13.320
Okay.
好吧。

1211
00:51:13.820 --> 00:51:17.020
I wanted to know what are king-size sheets called in England.
我想知道英国的特大号床单叫什么。

1212
00:51:17.280 --> 00:51:18.300
What are they called?
它们叫什么？

1213
00:51:18.780 --> 00:51:26.940
Well, the sheet sizes and bed sizes in England are called single, double, king, super king,
嗯，英国的床单和床的尺寸叫单人、双人、大号、超大号，

1214
00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:27.560
and emperor.
还有皇帝号。

1215
00:51:28.040 --> 00:51:28.520
Oh.
哦。

1216
00:51:28.860 --> 00:51:29.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1217
00:51:29.820 --> 00:51:30.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1218
00:51:30.320 --> 00:51:33.060
And none of them directly coordinate with American sizes.
而且它们和美国的尺寸完全对不上。

1219
00:51:33.720 --> 00:51:40.060
So if I bought a queen-size bedding set and moved to the UK, it would not work.
所以如果我买了套大号床品搬到英国，那是没法用的。

1220
00:51:40.060 --> 00:51:40.820
Throw it in the trash.
直接扔垃圾桶吧。

1221
00:51:40.960 --> 00:51:42.280
Throw it in the trash?
扔垃圾桶？

1222
00:51:42.440 --> 00:51:44.340
Maybe cut it up, use it for rags.
也许剪开当抹布用。

1223
00:51:44.720 --> 00:51:46.580
Well, it's not going to fit on your bed.
反正你的床上是用不了了。

1224
00:51:46.580 --> 00:51:47.340
What am I doing?
我在干什么？

1225
00:51:47.460 --> 00:51:48.360
Cutting up bed sheets.
剪床单。

1226
00:51:50.040 --> 00:51:55.560
If you rank the large beds by size, here's the order it would go in from smallest to largeSt.
如果按尺寸给大床排个序，从小到大依次是这样的。

1227
00:51:56.040 --> 00:51:56.280
Okay.
好。

1228
00:51:57.120 --> 00:51:57.580
King.
大号。

1229
00:51:57.820 --> 00:51:59.020
That's the smallest?
那是最小的？

1230
00:51:59.640 --> 00:52:01.180
Of the large beds.
在大床里是。

1231
00:52:01.440 --> 00:52:01.860
Okay.
好吧。

1232
00:52:02.420 --> 00:52:06.100
It goes king, super king, California king, emperor.
顺序是大号、超大号、加州大号、皇帝号。

1233
00:52:07.040 --> 00:52:12.780
The two beds that are closest in size is the British super king and the American California king.
尺寸最接近的两款床是英国的超大号和美国的加州大号。

1234
00:52:12.780 --> 00:52:20.240
They're both 71 inches wide, but the California king is much longer than the super king.
它们宽度都是71英寸，但加州大号比超大号长得多。

1235
00:52:20.840 --> 00:52:25.540
The emperor bed is seven feet wide and seven feet long.
皇帝号床有七英尺宽、七英尺长。

1236
00:52:25.920 --> 00:52:27.260
It's humongous.
那简直巨大。

1237
00:52:27.440 --> 00:52:28.500
Who's sleeping in that?
谁会睡那种床？

1238
00:52:29.100 --> 00:52:31.200
Professional basketball players, I think.
我想是职业篮球运动员吧。

1239
00:52:31.580 --> 00:52:32.160
Lots of people, I guess.
很多人吧，我猜。

1240
00:52:32.520 --> 00:52:33.640
I googled it.
我谷歌了一下。

1241
00:52:33.820 --> 00:52:37.160
The average professional basketball player is 6'6".
职业篮球运动员的平均身高是6英尺6英寸。

1242
00:52:37.160 --> 00:52:39.840
So this emperor bed would be perfect for them.
所以这张皇帝号床对他们来说正合适。

1243
00:52:39.940 --> 00:52:40.140
Yeah.
没错。

1244
00:52:40.260 --> 00:52:41.640
I can't believe I know that.
真不敢相信我竟然知道这些。

1245
00:52:41.640 --> 00:52:44.060
I mean, I really googled so much on this one, lady.
我是说，为了这个我真的谷歌了好多，女士。

1246
00:52:44.280 --> 00:52:46.140
Hey, get ready for your next cocktail party.
嘿，准备好迎接你的下一次鸡尾酒会吧。

1247
00:52:46.260 --> 00:52:47.360
You're going to be a delight.
你一定会大受欢迎的。

1248
00:52:47.620 --> 00:52:48.340
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1249
00:52:49.220 --> 00:52:52.500
There are more king beds than you could have ever imagined.
大号床的种类比你想象的还要多。

1250
00:52:53.100 --> 00:52:57.400
In America, there is more than just the king and the California king.
在美国，床的种类可不止大号和加州大号这两种。

1251
00:52:57.720 --> 00:53:04.840
There is the Alaskan king, the Wyoming king, and the Texas king, and they're all bigger than the California king.
有阿拉斯加特大号床、怀俄明特大号床，还有德克萨斯特大号床，它们都比加州特大号床还要大。

1252
00:53:05.200 --> 00:53:08.420
The Wyoming king is the same as an emperor bed in the UK.
怀俄明特大号床和英国的皇帝床是一样的。

1253
00:53:08.420 --> 00:53:11.480
Hey, the Alaskan king is the biggest bed.
嘿，阿拉斯加特大号床是最大的床。

